Cerberus TS is the Kotlin redevelopment of a framework originally published as
JeakBot / jeak-framework. Historical source files, documentation and assets are
preserved under legacy/ and are not part of the active build.

Original copyright notices are retained in LICENSE and the historical archive.
They record the project's origin and do not designate its current developer or
maintainer. Current development is performed by Cerberus Labs.

Cerberus TS is an independent TeamSpeak integration. TeamSpeak, Minecraft,
Bukkit and Paper names referenced in documentation identify their respective
products or APIs and do not imply affiliation.

Voice transport uses TS3J by Manevolent under Apache-2.0. PacketAead.kt adapts
TS3J's PacketTransformation to Kotlin and uses one AEAD operation per datagram
for compatibility with current Bouncy Castle releases. TS3J's license is in
docs/licenses/ts3j-APACHE-2.0.txt.

Opus encoding uses Concentus by Logan Stromberg and the Opus contributors.
Its license and copyright notices are in docs/licenses/concentus-LICENSE.txt.
FFmpeg and yt-dlp are external programs supplied by the operator; their binaries
are not bundled in this distribution.

Persistence uses Hibernate ORM 7.4.17.Final and HikariCP 7.1.0 under Apache-2.0,
and ClassGraph 5.0.0 by Luke Hutchison under MIT. Their licenses are in
docs/licenses/{hibernate,HikariCP,classgraph}-LICENSE.txt.
The unmodified MariaDB Connector/J 4.0.0 is supplied as a separate runtime JAR
under LGPL-2.1-or-later; its license is in docs/licenses/mariadb-connector-j-LICENSE.txt.
Corresponding upstream source: https://github.com/mariadb-corporation/mariadb-connector-j/tree/4.0.0
